  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "`appInfoLocalizations` represent your app’s localized metadata that is displayed in the App Store. You can create, read, update, and remove the localized metadata. It includes the following attributes for each localization:",
          "refs": []
        },
        {
          "text": "You can update localized metadata when your app is in an editable state. For more information about the metadata, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-app-information/localize-app-store-information`. For a list of supported languages, see `https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/app-store-localizations`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/manage-app-information/localize-app-store-information",
            "https://developer.apple.com/help/app-store-connect/reference/app-store-localizations"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "> **Note**\n>\n>  The languages you add to an `appInfoLocalizations` resource only affect your app’s metadata. To add languages to your app’s binary, see `https://help.apple.com/xcode/mac/current/#/deve2bc11fab`.",
          "refs": [
            "https://help.apple.com/xcode/mac/current/#/deve2bc11fab"
          ]
        }
      ],
